This is "What era of Samurai is this?" problem.

"Samurai-Era" started late Heian-era (about A.D.1000) and
ended Edo-era(A.D.1867)(did you see "The Last Samurai"? :-)).
But well-known active Samurai-Era are Sengoku(civil war)-era
(about A.D.1550-1600) and Edo-era (A.D.1603-1867).
Most of Samurai-movies and novels are on either era.

"Hatamoto" is the rank made on Edo-era.
But Edo-era is pretty peaceful and conservative,
so anyone barely promote own rank.
So I assumed that Samurai of NetHack is one of Sengoku-era
(a footman unified all over the nation) and decided to
delete "Hatamoto".

I agreed that "Shogun" should be deleted.
But adding "Samurai" as the rank is doubtful.
This cause simple and difficult question, "What's Samurai?".

